        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli-runner): restore history for SQLite-backed CLI resumes",
        "body": "Related: #98236\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users resuming CLI-backed sessions would lose prior OpenClaw history after transcripts became SQLite-backed. Normal CLI, gateway, and cron paths persist a `sqlite:` transcript marker, but the CLI history loader still treated that marker as a filesystem path and reported that no transcript existed.\n\nThe same symptom could recur after moving a supported state-directory backup to a different absolute path because persisted markers retain the old path even though the restored per-agent database is now authoritative at the new location.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe CLI runner now recognizes SQLite transcript markers, validates their session and agent identity, and reads from the current canonical store through the storage-neutral session accessor. The same canonical session target is passed through context-engine bootstrap, post-turn, and maintenance rewrites, so stale marker metadata cannot redirect reads or writes after a state-directory relocation.\n\nThe accessor streams only the newest complete rows within the existing 5 MiB JSONL-compatible window, restores the session envelope when the tail is truncated, and preserves migration, branch-safety, active-leaf selection, and message-cap behavior. Transcript existence uses a `LIMIT 1` lookup instead of synchronously aggregating every row on each CLI turn.\n\nThe previous short-header-read proposal and regression were intentionally removed as part of this PR redirect; this PR is now scoped to SQLite-backed CLI history restoration.\n\nThis is distinct from #108851, which bounds gateway message pagination through a derived active-message projection; it does not repair the CLI runner's marker existence or raw-history path. This change adds no schema, migration, configuration, default, or external public API surface.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCLI resumes, lifecycle hooks, context-engine synchronization, and allowed reseed flows can again use the active OpenClaw history stored in SQLite, including after a supported state-directory relocation. Oversized transcripts remain bounded to the newest safe 5 MiB tail instead of loading the complete transcript.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Initial RED on the test-first commit: [run](https://github.com/mushuiyu886/openclaw/actions/runs/29512957643), [job](https://github.com/mushuiyu886/openclaw/actions/runs/29512957643/job/87670775318) — 27 passed, 2 failed; marker existence returned `false` and oversized SQLite history returned `[]`.\n- Review-gap RED: [run](https://github.com/mushuiyu886/openclaw/actions/runs/29520108279), [job](https://github.com/mushuiyu886/openclaw/actions/runs/29520108279/job/87694811630) — 31 passed, 2 failed; the relocated marker was rejected and existence still invoked full transcript stats.\n- Memory-bound RED: [run](https://github.com/mushuiyu886/openclaw/actions/runs/29522181652), [job](https://github.com/mushuiyu886/openclaw/actions/runs/29522181652/job/87701667581) — tail selection still requested `event_json`, so an over-budget row was materialized before the JavaScript byte check.\n- Context-target RED: [run](https://github.com/mushuiyu886/openclaw/actions/runs/29524447512), [job](https://github.com/mushuiyu886/openclaw/actions/runs/29524447512/job/87709238990) — the runtime transcript target still resolved a relocated session to the stale marker path.\n- Final GREEN on exact fix head `666f9b33ca5b1fd1df80078c4c9de612b595f1de`: [run](https://github.com/mushuiyu886/openclaw/actions/runs/29525223602), [job](https://github.com/mushuiyu886/openclaw/actions/runs/29525223602/job/87711899882) — 5 test files and 133 tests passed across the runtime-config and agents shards.\n- Local Node 22.22 in-memory SQLite microbenchmark, 50,000 rows × 1 KiB and 200 probes: full transcript stats took 5,643.8 ms versus 0.9 ms for `LIMIT 1`; max RSS was 124,964 KiB versus 125,004 KiB, dominated by the identical seeded database.\n- Targeted `oxfmt --check` and `oxlint` for the changed CLI/session-accessor/context-maintenance files — passed with 0 warnings and 0 errors in the same exact-head job.\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.core.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core.tsbuildinfo` — passed in the same exact-head job.\n- `git diff --check b8b064a9483ee0917648207ffe91438a2da8c828 HEAD` — passed in the same exact-head job.\n- `codex review --base upstream/main` — completed; one P2 requested restoring the superseded file-backed short-header fix. It was not applied because this PR was explicitly redirected to SQLite-backed CLI history and the final diff no longer claims that older case; no actionable finding targeted the SQLite or context-engine changes.\n\nVerification covers the OpenClaw SQLite transcript-to-CLI-history production path on GitHub-hosted Ubuntu. It does not exercise a real third-party CLI/provider, browser, or cross-platform runtime.\n",
